# Clean Code

Prefer:

- intention-revealing names
- small cohesive functions/modules
- explicit dependencies
- immutable data where practical
- composition over inheritance
- narrow interfaces
- domain-specific types
- early returns over deeply nested branching
- removal of duplication in business rules

Avoid:

- god classes/modules
- boolean flag arguments
- primitive obsession
- hidden global state
- speculative abstraction
- dead code
- comments that restate code
- catch-all utility modules with unrelated responsibilities

Refactoring must preserve externally observable behavior.
